synopsis: "PostgreSQL store for sanctions-screening, over pg-async"
description:
  "Store_pg implements sanctions-screening's Store.S (list versions, subjects, screening results and case events, all idempotent) on PostgreSQL through pg-async, with embedded migrations, inside its own schema (with its own migrations table). Needs libpq."
